>2005</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>5363</fpage><lpage>5371</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16086453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McShan</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Symbolic inference of xenobiotics metabolism</article-title><source>Pac. Symp. Biocomput</source><year>2004</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>545</fpage><lpage>556</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14992532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nobeli</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Thornton</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A bioinformatician's view of the metabolome</article-title><source>BioEssays</source><year>2006</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>534</fpage><lpage>545</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16615085</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Systematic analysis of enzyme-catalyzed reaction patterns and prediction of microbial biodegradation pathways</article-title><source>J. Chem. Inf. Model.</source><year>2007</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>1702</fpage><lpage>1712</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17516640</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stockwell</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chemical genetics: ligand-based discovery of gene function</article-title><source>Nat. Rev. Genet.</source><year>2000</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>116</fpage><lpage>125</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11253651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group p